<xs:schema targetNamespace="http://www.sdmx.org/resources/sdmxml/schemas/v3_1/structure"
			xmlns="http://www.sdmx.org/resources/sdmxml/schemas/v3_1/structure"
			xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
			xmlns:common="http://www.sdmx.org/resources/sdmxml/schemas/v3_1/common"
			xmlns:structure="http://www.sdmx.org/resources/sdmxml/schemas/v3_1/structure"
			elementFormDefault="qualified">

	<xs:import namespace="http://www.sdmx.org/resources/sdmxml/schemas/v3_1/common" schemaLocation="SDMXCommon.xsd"/>

	<xs:include schemaLocation="SDMXStructureBase.xsd"/>

	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:appinfo>SDMX Custom Structure Definition Module</xs:appinfo>
		<xs:documentation>The custom structure definition module defines the structure of custom structure definition (CSD) constructs. A custom structure definition allows an agency to define the schema of a new maintainable structure type which does not exist in the SDMX Information Model. Instances conforming to a custom structure definition are validated against a dynamically generated schema derived from the definition.</xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>

	<xs:complexType abstract="true" name="CustomStructureDefinitionBaseType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomStructureDefinitionBaseType is an abstract base type that forms the basis for the CustomStructureDefinitionType. It extends the maintainable type to add the definition of the instance content model: an optional items declaration, a collection of properties and property choices, and a collection of locally defined custom types.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="common:MaintainableType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Items" type="ItemsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Items declares the item type for a custom structure definition whose base is ItemScheme. It is required when the base attribute is ItemScheme and must not be used otherwise. The declared property in instances is always named 'items' and may occur zero or more times. The referenced custom type must extend (directly or transitively) the Nameable base, as it plays the role of the Item. Instances of an item scheme based custom structure inherit the isPartial behaviour of item schemes. Hierarchical items are not implicit; if a hierarchy is required, it must be modelled explicitly in the custom type, for example with a property that takes a collection of the item type.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:element name="Property" type="PropertyType">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>Property defines a single property of instances of the custom structure definition.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
						<xs:element name="PropertyChoice" type="PropertyChoiceType">
							<xs:annotation>
								<xs:documentation>PropertyChoice defines a set of mutually exclusive properties; each occurrence of the choice in an instance is exactly one of the child properties.</xs:documentation>
							</xs:annotation>
						</xs:element>
					</xs:choice>
					<xs:element name="CustomType" type="LocalCustomTypeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>CustomType defines a reusable complex type which is local to this custom structure definition, and which may be used as the representation of properties via a CustomTypeReference.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
				<xs:attribute name="classType" type="ClassNameType" use="required">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>The classType attribute holds the class name used in the URN of instances of this custom structure definition (e.g. PivotTable). It is decoupled from the identifier of the definition; the maintenance agency is responsible for ensuring that the same class name is not used by two different custom structure definitions which it maintains.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:attribute>
				<xs:attribute name="base" type="CustomStructureBaseType" use="optional" default="Maintainable">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>The base attribute indicates the SDMX base type of instances of this custom structure definition. Instances are always maintainable artefacts (agency, id, version, and name as a minimum). If the base is ItemScheme, the Items element must be provided.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:attribute>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="CustomStructureDefinitionType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomStructureDefinitionType describes the structure of a custom structure definition. A custom structure definition declares the content model (properties, choices of properties, and locally defined custom types) to which instances of the custom structure must conform.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:restriction base="CustomStructureDefinitionBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element ref="common:Annotations" minOccurs="0"/>
					<xs:element ref="common:Link" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
					<xs:element ref="common:Name" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
					<xs:element ref="common:Description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
					<xs:element name="Items" type="ItemsType" minOccurs="0"/>
					<xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:element name="Property" type="PropertyType"/>
						<xs:element name="PropertyChoice" type="PropertyChoiceType"/>
					</xs:choice>
					<xs:element name="CustomType" type="LocalCustomTypeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:unique name="CustomType_UniqueProperty">
							<xs:selector xpath="structure:Property | structure:PropertyChoice/structure:Property"/>
							<xs:field xpath="@id"/>
						</xs:unique>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
				<xs:attribute name="urn" type="common:CustomStructureDefinitionUrnType" use="optional"/>
			</xs:restriction>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="CustomStructureBaseType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomStructureBaseType provides an enumeration of the SDMX base types available to a custom structure definition.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
			<xs:enumeration value="Maintainable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Instances are plain maintainable artefacts.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ItemScheme">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Instances are item schemes; the Items element of the definition declares the item type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:simpleType name="ClassNameType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ClassNameType restricts the format of a class name used for URN generation. By convention class names are in camel case starting with an upper case letter (e.g. PivotTable), although this is not enforced.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:NCName">
			<xs:pattern value="[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="ItemsType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ItemsType declares the item type of an item scheme based custom structure definition. The property which holds the items in instances is always identified as 'items' and may occur zero or more times.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:attribute name="type" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The type attribute references a custom type defined in this custom structure definition which plays the Item role. The referenced type must extend (directly or transitively) the Nameable base.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="PropertyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>PropertyType describes a single property of instances of a custom structure definition or of a custom type. The property identifier becomes an element name in the dynamically generated instance schema and is therefore restricted to the NCNameIDType. Exactly one representation must be supplied for the property.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="common:Name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Name provides a human-readable name documenting the property. This may be provided in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="common:Description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Description provides a longer human-readable description of the property. This may be provided in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:choice>
				<xs:element name="ValueFormat" type="TextFormatType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>ValueFormat describes a value property with a primitive or higher level text type (e.g. String, Boolean, Integer, ObservationalTimePeriod), optionally restricted with the standard SDMX facets (minValue, maxValue, minLength, maxLength, pattern, decimals, etc.).</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="Reference" type="ReferencePropertyType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Reference describes a reference property; in instances the property holds the URN of the referenced artefact.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="IndirectReference" type="IndirectReferencePropertyType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>IndirectReference describes a string property which holds the identifier of an object that is resolved against the context established by another reference property of the instance (e.g. a dimension identifier resolved against the dataflow referenced by a sibling property). This allows a system to validate that the referenced object exists and to support reference resolution and referential integrity.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="CustomTypeReference" type="CustomTypeReferenceType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>CustomTypeReference describes a property whose representation is a custom type defined in this custom structure definition. A custom type may reference itself or its containing type, allowing recursive structures (e.g. an explicit hierarchy of items).</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="MultilingualText" type="MultilingualTextPropertyType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>MultilingualText describes a property which holds a text value in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms, without requiring the containing type to be nameable.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
			</xs:choice>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="id" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The id attribute holds the identifier of the property. Because property identifiers are used to create XML elements in the dynamically generated instance schemas, they must be compliant with the NCName type in XML Schema. Property identifiers must be unique within their containing custom structure definition or custom type. The identifiers 'items' (the items property of item scheme based custom structures) and 'CustomStructureDefinition' (the mandatory reference of every instance to its defining custom structure definition) are reserved.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="minOccurs" type="xs:nonNegativeInteger" use="optional" default="1">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The minOccurs attribute indicates the minimum number of values that must be reported for the property. A minimum of 1 (the default) makes the property mandatory.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="maxOccurs" type="common:OccurenceType" use="optional" default="1">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The maxOccurs attribute indicates the maximum number of values that can be reported for the property. It may be given the value 'unbounded'.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="PropertyChoiceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>PropertyChoiceType describes a set of mutually exclusive properties. Each occurrence of the choice in an instance is exactly one of the child properties; as elsewhere in the SDMX schemas, the choice is between differently named properties which may have different representations. The cardinality of the choice group is governed by the minOccurs and maxOccurs attributes of the choice itself; the occurrence attributes of the child properties are not used.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Property" type="PropertyType" minOccurs="2" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="minOccurs" type="xs:nonNegativeInteger" use="optional" default="1">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The minOccurs attribute indicates the minimum number of occurrences of the choice group. A minimum of 1 (the default) makes the choice mandatory.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="maxOccurs" type="common:OccurenceType" use="optional" default="1">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The maxOccurs attribute indicates the maximum number of occurrences of the choice group. It may be given the value 'unbounded'.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="ReferencePropertyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ReferencePropertyType describes the representation of a reference property. The target may be restricted to a class of SDMX artefacts (targetClass), to instances of a custom structure definition (targetCsd), or locked to one specific artefact (Target). Exactly one of targetClass and targetCsd should be provided; if neither is provided the property is fully open and may reference any SDMX identifiable (equivalent to a targetClass of Any).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Target" type="common:UrnReferenceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Target locks the property to one specific artefact by URN reference, including a reference to an instance of a custom structure definition. The standard reference version forms are supported, including wildcarded and late binding version references.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="targetClass" type="ObjectClassType" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The targetClass attribute restricts the class of SDMX artefacts which may be referenced by the property.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="targetCsd" type="common:CustomStructureDefinitionReferenceType" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The targetCsd attribute restricts the property to reference instances of the referenced custom structure definition, which may be this definition or one maintained by any agency.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="IndirectReferencePropertyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>IndirectReferencePropertyType describes the representation of an indirect reference property. The property value is the identifier of an object of the target class, resolved against the context established by the reference property named by the scope attribute.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:attribute name="targetClass" type="ObjectClassType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The targetClass attribute indicates the class of the object identified by the property value (e.g. Dimension, Code).</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="scope" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The scope attribute holds the identifier of the reference property which establishes the resolution context. This may be a sibling property, or, from within a custom type, a property defined at the root level of the custom structure definition.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="CustomTypeReferenceType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomTypeReferenceType describes the representation of a property whose value is a complex structure conforming to a custom type defined in the same custom structure definition.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:attribute name="type" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The type attribute references a custom type defined in this custom structure definition by its identifier.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="MultilingualTextPropertyType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>MultilingualTextPropertyType describes the representation of a multilingual text property. In instances the property holds a text value in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms; the occurrence attributes of the property are interpreted per language.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="LocalCustomTypeType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomTypeType describes a complex type defined locally within a custom structure definition. A custom type extends one of the abstract SDMX bases (Annotatable, Identifiable, Nameable) or another custom type defined in the same custom structure definition. The extends and extendsType attributes are mutually exclusive; if neither is provided the type extends Annotatable. Extension is additive only: a subtype adds properties and must not redefine or restrict inherited ones, and extension chains must be acyclic.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element ref="common:Name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Name provides a human-readable name documenting the custom type. This may be provided in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element ref="common:Description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Description provides a longer human-readable description of the custom type. This may be provided in multiple, parallel language-equivalent forms.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:element name="Property" type="PropertyType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>Property defines a single property of the custom type.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
				<xs:element name="PropertyChoice" type="PropertyChoiceType">
					<xs:annotation>
						<xs:documentation>PropertyChoice defines a set of mutually exclusive properties of the custom type.</xs:documentation>
					</xs:annotation>
				</xs:element>
			</xs:choice>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="id" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The id attribute holds the identifier of the custom type, which must be unique within the custom structure definition.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="extends" type="ExtensibleBaseType" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The extends attribute indicates the abstract SDMX base type which this custom type extends. It must not be used together with the extendsType attribute. ItemScheme is not a valid base for a custom type; it is only available at the level of the custom structure definition itself.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="extendsType" type="common:NCNameIDType" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The extendsType attribute references, by identifier, another custom type defined in the same custom structure definition which this custom type extends. It must not be used together with the extends attribute.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
		<xs:attribute name="classType" type="ClassNameType" use="optional">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>The classType attribute holds the class name used for the automatic generation of URNs of objects of this type within an instance (e.g. PivotTableRow). It is required when the custom type extends, directly or transitively, Identifiable or Nameable, and must not be used for purely annotatable types. Each type in an extension chain must declare its own, unique class name so that generated URNs remain unique.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="ExtensibleBaseType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ExtensibleBaseType provides an enumeration of the abstract SDMX base types which a custom type may extend.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
			<xs:enumeration value="Annotatable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The type carries only annotations in addition to its declared properties.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="Identifiable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The type has an identifier and a generated URN in addition to annotations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="Nameable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The type has an identifier, a generated URN, a multilingual name, and an optional multilingual description in addition to annotations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="CustomStructuresType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>CustomStructuresType describes the structure of the container for instances of custom structure definitions. Each instance is an element in the namespace given by the URN of the custom structure definition to which it conforms, with the element name being the class name of the definition (e.g. an element PivotTable in the namespace urn:sdmx:org.sdmx.infomodel.csd.CustomStructureDefinition=IMF:PIVOT_TABLE(1.0.0)). Each instance also carries a mandatory CustomStructureDefinition element which references, by URN, the custom structure definition to which it conforms; the dynamically generated schema fixes this value to the URN of the definition, guaranteeing it agrees with the namespace. Because the namespace and reference include the version of the definition, instances conforming to different versions of the same definition may coexist in one message. The content is processed laxly: a validator equipped with the dynamically generated schemas of the custom structure definitions it knows (see the schema generation rules) validates the instances in full, while a validator with only the standard SDMX schema set checks well-formedness only.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:any namespace="##other" processContents="lax" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="ObjectClassType">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>ObjectClassType provides a comprehensive enumeration of the classes of SDMX artefacts which may be the target of a reference property, together with the open values Any, AnyMaintainable, and AnyIdentifiable.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
			<xs:enumeration value="Any">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Any SDMX identifiable or maintainable object, including instances of custom structure definitions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AnyIdentifiable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Any SDMX identifiable object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AnyMaintainable">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Any SDMX maintainable object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="Agency"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="AgencyScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="AttributeDescriptor"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Categorisation"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Category"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CategoryScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CategorySchemeMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Code"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Codelist"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Concept"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ConceptScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ConceptSchemeMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CustomStructureDefinition"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CustomType"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="CustomTypeScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataAttribute"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataConstraint"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataConsumer"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataConsumerScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Dataflow"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataProvider"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataProviderScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DataStructure"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DatePatternMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Dimension"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DimensionDescriptor"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="EpochMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="FrequencyFormatMapping"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="GroupDimensionDescriptor"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="HierarchicalCode"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Hierarchy"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="HierarchyAssociation"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Level"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Measure"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MeasureDescriptor"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataAttribute"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataConstraint"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Metadataflow"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataProvider"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataProviderScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataProvisionAgreement"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataSet"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="MetadataStructure"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="NamePersonalisation"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="NamePersonalisationScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OrganisationSchemeMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OrganisationUnit"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="OrganisationUnitScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Process"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ProcessStep"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ProvisionAgreement"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ReportingCategory"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ReportingTaxonomy"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ReportingTaxonomyMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="RepresentationMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Ruleset"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="RulesetScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="StructureMap"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="TimeDimension"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Transformation"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="TransformationScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Transition"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="UserDefinedOperator"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="UserDefinedOperatorScheme"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="ValueList"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="VtlCodelistMapping"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="VtlConceptMapping"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="VtlDataflowMapping"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="VtlMappingScheme"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

</xs:schema>
